{"actor": "opencode", "data": {"summary": "I overwrote this VM's ~/.gitconfig while building the T-0024 falsification harness: two of its three cases passed Path.home() as the sandbox HOME, so the harness wrote its throwaway gitconfig over the real one and destroyed user.name, user.email, and credential.helper. Repaired from the values read earlier in the same session (bot identity confirmed against 125 committed commits); git credential fill now exits 0. The harness caused it, not the environment: my first reading of the 'invalid credential line' error blamed the App arrangement, and that reading was wrong - the corrupted gitconfig pointed credential.helper at /tmp/github-app-jwt.sh, a JWT generator that is not a credential helper, which is exactly what produced the warning. Every case now gets its own HOME under the harness directory, asserted before any write."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "note", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 5, "session": "2026-10-03-040-make-origin-doctor-read-the-push-credent", "ts": "2026-10-03T23:48:30+00:00"}
